        "prob_desc_description": "Tanechka is shopping in the toy shop. There are exactly $$$n$$$ toys in the shop for sale, the cost of the $$$i$$$-th toy is $$$i$$$ burles. She wants to choose two toys in such a way that their total cost is $$$k$$$ burles. How many ways to do that does she have?Each toy appears in the shop exactly once. Pairs $$$(a, b)$$$ and $$$(b, a)$$$ are considered equal. Pairs $$$(a, b)$$$, where $$$a=b$$$, are not allowed.",
